+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Confirmed Porter II EV selects c3-pht-porter; 2022–24 Ioniq 5 HDA2 selects c3-pht. A different branch requires Park, four zero-speed wheels for one second and Panda noOutput during startup, then checkout and reboot, vehicle settings and recalibration on actual vehicle changes. No mid-drive switching.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Enable and restart on the Porter first to save its seven-setting baseline. Power down before moving the device and use the matching harness. Initial installation of the other branch requires internet and a parkhantae/openpilot remote; compatible installed local branches can switch offline.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Local edits, conflicts, mismatched handoff code or unresolved identity hold control without a forced reset. Inspect AutoVehicleBranchStatus for progress. OFF applies at the next startup; an in-progress handoff must complete an OS reboot. This feature does not guarantee stop hold or vehicle acceptance of automatic SET.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
